{"tool_name":"fmcsr","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"fmcsr","home":"https://bioconductor.org/packages/fmcsR","license":"Artistic-2.0","summary":"The fmcsR package introduces an efficient maximum common substructure (MCS) algorithms combined with a novel matching strategy that allows for atom and/or bond mismatches in the substructures shared among two small molecules. The resulting flexible MCSs (FMCSs) are often larger than strict MCSs, resulting in the identification of more common features in their source structures, as well as a higher sensitivity in finding compounds with weak structural similarities. The fmcsR package provides several utilities to use the FMCS algorithm for pairwise compound comparisons, structure similarity searching and clustering.","addition_date":"2017-01-17T14:59:10Z","last_update_date":"2026-08-30T02:14:33.414600Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Library"],"version":["1.54.0"],"collections":["BioConductor"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:fmcsr","credit":[{"name":"Kevin Horan"},{"name":"Thomas Girke"},{"name":"Tyler Backman"},{"name":"Yan Wang"}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://bioconductor.org/packages/fmcsR"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Small molecule structure","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1463"},"format":[{"term":"Tertiary structure format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2033"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Clustering","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3432"},{"term":"Structure comparison","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2483"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Chemical structure image","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1712"},"format":[{"term":"Image format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3547"},{"term":"Textual format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2330"}]},{"data":{"term":"Database search results","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2080"},"format":[{"term":"Image format","uri":